  "term": "primary mood disorder",
  "definition": "A primary mood disorder is a mood disorder considered a separate condition in its own right, rather than one occurring in the context of epilepsy. In the source, it is contrasted with mood disorders seen in people with epilepsy, although treatment is described as the same.",
